openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/design.md:3:See `proposal.md` for the experiment motivation. The existing pure retrieval canonicalizer already returns a normalized source query plus at most one alternate, and hybrid retrieval searches both representations, deduplicates each modality by LD id, and applies existing RRF once per modality. The matcher sends the original source query, not the alternate, to DeepSeek reranking. The harness calibration recognizes explicit standard ball-valve execution as a standard-bore requirement, and catalog product text can express that requirement as `стандартнопроходной` or `стандартный проход`.
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/design.md:24:Extend the existing canonicalization boundary only when the query contains a supported ball-valve anchor and an explicit standard-execution or standard-passage phrase. Add the catalog lexical variants `стандартнопроходной` and `стандартный проход` to the existing canonical text rather than replacing source wording. Before emitting the alternate, detect explicit full-passage or reduced-passage wording and decline the standard-bore expansion if either is present.
